<p>Minneapolis-based {% place "peavey-company" %}F. H. Peavey &amp; Company{% endplace %} purchased Russell-Miller and its 140 county elevators, terminals, and flour mills in 1954. Renamed Peavey Company in 1962, it was acquired by {% place "conagra" %}ConAgra Inc.{% endplace %} in 1982. ConAgra is now the largest flour miller in the USA.</p>

<p>Intermittent flooding and the economies offered by larger facilities led the Mandan mill to close in 1956. Its buildings were demolished during the winter of 1963–64. The land was given to the {% place "city-of-mandan" %}City of Mandan{% endplace %} and became its maintenance shop and outdoor equipment-storage yard.</p>

